{"type":"plan","title":"The Mended Kite","logline":"A gust tears a child's kite, and a grandfather's sailor's seam stitches it back to flight.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Dawn light over Brighton pier; Maya stands on the shingle beach holding the string of her red kite, which soars high above the wooden railings. Gentle waves roll in, morning wind ruffles her raincoat.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[1,3]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"A sudden gust slams the kite into the pier railings; the red sail rips from corner to corner, a jagged hole with a flap hanging down, sky visible through the tear.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[1,4]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya runs along the seafront toward home, the broken kite hugged to her chest, wind whipping her hair; the pier and sea stretch behind her in morning light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[1,3,4]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Morning light streams through lace curtains onto the wooden table; Grandfather lowers his newspaper, eyes widening as Maya bursts in with the torn kite.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[2,5]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"At the vintage table Grandfather spreads the kite flat, threads a needle with sailcloth thread, the kettle steaming beside jars; morning sun highlights the wooden grain.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[2,3,4,5]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle over the table shows Grandfather pointing at each stitch, Maya leaning in to watch; the patched white cloth with visible stitches now covers the hole.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[2,4,5]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Close-up on Maya's hand as she paints a bold gold star onto the white patch; the brush strokes catch the morning light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[2,4,5]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Bright afternoon sun bathes the pier and shingle beach; Maya and Grandfather walk side by side, the starred kite tucked under Grandfather's arm, sea sparkling.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[1,4]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Low angle from the sand shows Maya sprinting into the wind, the kite climbing higher than ever above the rolling waves, string taut in her hand.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[1,4,6]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya extends the string to Grandfather; he takes it, his face breaking into a boyish laugh as the kite dances overhead in the afternoon breeze.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[1,4]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Golden dusk glows over the sand as Maya and Grandfather stroll home along the beach, the mended starred kite resting on Maya's shoulder; the pier silhouettes against the amber sky.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[1,4,6]}]}
